==Strategy==
Compared to the original Floor 47, this stage on the other hand is suspiciously relaxed. Without the presence of Brollows to obliterate your rushers and the general decreased number of enemies per wave, this stage shouldn't be too difficult to clear. Nevertheless, many of the original Floor 47 strategies still remain true here. Spamming Research Combos alongside Rock is usually enough to stall both Corrupted Moneko and Puffsley in place, while you use attackers to chip down each enemy here. Additionally, you will want Shield Piercing units like Cat Researcher or Supercar to obliterate the Ackey, as its increased health and Multi-Hit makes it extremely annoying to deal with.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Research Rock claims another stage, as Rock here is able to stall both bosses, bait out Peng hits, and even kill Miz Devil once its Shield breaks.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: Hitman should be used for cleanup, but his general damage and LD is okay enough to get a bit of chip against Condemend Peng.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Slime maintains its usefulness here, being able to charge into the frontlines and get out cheap damage for little to no effort. Slime's Wave is also long enough to hit a Condemned Peng in the back. Note that Miz Devil's Shield will tank both Slime's initial hit and its subsequent Wave, so make sure to run something to kill Miz Devil once that happens.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] or [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: Either one of these units (or an Uber) will be needed to deal with the Ackey in a timely manner. Cat Researcher is much less punishing and is also easier to obtain, but Supercar having enough damage to one-shot Ackey makes it the better option if you happen to own it.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can does not work against Condemned Peng, but it's Can Can so somehow it's good here anyways. Use Can Can mainly for getting off nuke damage against Corrupted Moneko or Puffsley during the cleanup phase of the stage.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Fast rusher with damage. Bullet Train should mainly be used to hit Condemned Peng.
*[[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]]: A boosted KoL has very good damage for its 1 KB, allowing him to work well enough against the Condemned Peng.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut is able to get insane value here, being able to get huge damage off on the bosses and also having enough damage to obliterate a Condemned Peng. So long as you aren't sending Bahamut directly into a Death Surge or when Ackey is attacking, Bahamut will be good enough to wipe out an entire enemy wave. It is possible to chain Puffsley's Comet at the start of the stage, see guide below for a more in depth explanation.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]: Doron is a cheap suicide unit who can get some nice damage off against the Peng and Miz Devil.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Nukers for either Traitless or Alien are good here so you can beat the stage fast(er). Examples include [[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]], [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]], [[Mekako Saionji (Uber Rare Cat)|Mission Control Mekako]], and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]].
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Balrog Balrogs all over this stage about as much as he did the original Floor 47. See the Walkthrough section for a showcase of how much Balrog nukes this stage.

